# Why: keep secrets, build artefacts and machine-local state out of git.
# The single most important line in this file is `.env` — see docs/08-security-model.md.
# A leaked .env in a security company's repo is an extinction-level event.

# --- Secrets (NEVER commit) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Node / Next.js ---
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Editors / OS ---
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Local infra state ---
docker-data/
*.log
